{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/828221-gathering-ideas-for-a-dark-era-could-use-some-some-discussion","id":828221,"title":"Gathering ideas for a Dark Era, could use some some discussion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-11T07:59:28-08:00","id":828221,"title":"Gathering ideas for a Dark Era, could use some some discussion","content":"Hello everyone, as the title suggests, I need some help. There's a Beast Dark Era I've been thinking about since I read the game and, even if I won't start writing it nowhere in the near future, I want to put down the basic structure so I can keep it in mind and elaborate on it as time goes on. Writing a Dark Era is no easy task (especially writing a <i>good </i>one) and while I'm not sure to be up to it, I'm certain that having some discussion about it with you will be quite helpful.<br /> <br /> The Dark Era I'm talking about is the Congo Free State one I've been annoying people about for ages. Essentially &quot;Beast meets Heart of Darkness&quot;. It will touch the whole period of King Leopold's rule, but the main focus will be the phase where rubber became the greatest objective of the colonization. A moment where, to be blunt, an already horrible situation took a turn for the worse.<br /> <br /> What I'm asking for is criticism, ideas, suggestions, requests, plot hooks for Beast and other gamelines or really any sort of comment you might have.<br /> <br /> The preliminary theme and mood are the following:<br /> <br /> <b>Theme: &quot;Savagery Hidden Within&quot;</b><br /> No matter who you were or the place you came from, living in King Leopold's Congo was an experience nobody was prepared about. Natives, agents of the colonial companies, missionaries, explorers and reporters...all agreed that the moment you became part of the nightmarish picture created to satisfy the demands of the colonial machine was as if entering another world. Given free reign and the excuse to behave anyway they want as long as they obtain results, with almost no judgment whatsoever, respectable gentlemen turn into monsters and brothers betray brothers. It's all more primal here, the norms of society abandoned in favor of impulses and will of survival. The only true rules are those made by the strong and the deeper you go along the river, the easier becomes to you distance yourself from civilization. Empathy is a virtue and, sometimes, a luxury, that's dangerously easy to loose along the way. The dissonance between boasted dignity and manifest savagery is ever-present. The fact that much of it is spawned by the very same dictates of the so-called civil society only makes it more jarring. Ultimately, every single person is left struggling with her darker instincts, having to fight the impulse to embrace the beast that dwells inside.<br /> <br /> <b>Mood: &quot;Waking Nightmare&quot;</b><br /> In Congo, one has to wonder where reality ends and where the Primordial Dream seeps in. The sheer magnitude of atrocities and horrors one can witness and that are carried on as if it's the norm is insane. Much of the population seems trapped into a narrative they unconsciously became part of and the few who notice either cannot do much or eventually fall for it as well.<br /> <br /> Then there's some snippets, ideas and miscellanea that I came up with to characterize the Era:<br /> - No easy answers. There's no such thing as &quot;bad guys VS good guys&quot;. It's all very, very grey. Absolute morality is tricky here, everyone's alone with himself and the only elements that speak about their valor are their actions. By default, you are alone in the darkness and you can only hope to find support in your...<br /> - ...Family. Which, then again, might not be easy. You don't choose it after all and in this era of clashing cultures its members come from all the sides. Native Beasts and Beasts from abroad (the same goes for all supernaturals of course) often have a hard time finding a common ground and they are torn between their human culture and Beastly nature. With the factions fragmented even within themselves, learning to accept your family is complicated.<br /> - Lots of Heroes, many of them of the bad kind. The cultural context makes it far too easy to embark on the kind of heroic crusade Beasts are afraid of. Good Heroes still exist, but a damaged individual that becomes a Hero is still a damaged individual. And there's plenty of those around here. It almost seems as the Primordial Dream is close to the waking world in King Leopold's Congo and such proximity has its consequences.<br /> - African Supernaturals. Faeries, vampires, spirits and everything else. Geist Kreves based on the cult of the ancestors, wereleopards and Hunter Compacts appropriate to the settings. You get the idea. Plenty of material to work with here.<br /> - Mokele-mbembe, as in the Beast behind the legend, is the Apex. He was on the verge of becoming an Incarnate but then came the Belgian domination and everything it brought along. Previously a lonely and powerful Beast, Mokele delayed his ascension in order to deal with his Family members, both local and foreign. Even if he's not eager too admit it, the events of the Era made him look back at his mortal identity and allegiances, something he thought to be ready to leave behind.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Working on the Theme. Leestsepeak expressed some legitimate and worrisome doubts about it so the I'm changing the &quot;first draft&quot; above","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-12-2016, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T08:21:03-08:00","id":828229,"title":"","content":"I would very much dwell in to Awakened side of the deal - <b>If Diamond Orders. as we know it, then before Sleepers colonization? </b>Or only local Nameless Traditions of Natives, having shock by being contrasted with &quot;white&quot; mages culture?<br /> <br /> In history of India Awakened, there are <b>two</b> Consilia in <i>Delhi</i> - one original Hindu, from local Orders created just after Alexanders death, -and British one, for white colonists. Two totally separated Awakened communities.<br /> <br /> Also, whole 1800's are Nameless War Era, so maybe Congo's fight for liberty is reflected in that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:38:11-08:00","id":828409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/828221-gathering-ideas-for-a-dark-era-could-use-some-some-discussion?p=828229#post828229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would very much dwell in to Awakened side of the deal - <b>If Diamond Orders. as we know it, then before Sleepers colonization? </b>Or only local Nameless Traditions of Natives, having shock by being contrasted with &quot;white&quot; mages culture?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something worth keeping in mind, yeah. Not that I have decided anything about it yet, but you make a good point about it being something that needs to be addressed.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-11T13:48:12-08:00","id":828419,"title":"","content":"Probably it will be more clear when we will see<i> To the Strongest </i>Mage Era - <b>DaveB</b> mentioned that will put some light of Nameless and lower Cults of that time in extra words.<br /> <br /> Mutapa Empire examples will also help with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T12:50:49-08:00","id":828924,"title":"","content":"Anything else? Really, read this as a brainstorming thread. Everything that comes to your mind about this topic, even criticism (hell, <i>especially</i> criticism) is welcomed and appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T14:46:59-08:00","id":828958,"title":"","content":"I think something worth keeping in mind about the Awakened is that Dave has implied the Awakened of Europe were well aware of their native counterparts in the Americas via the Astral Realm, so I really don't think it makes much sense for there to be African Mages entirely cut off from the Diamond.<br /> <br /> There might be those who refused involvement, or it might be that those members of the Diamond who were already present have to navigate the situation, but Africans and Europeans have been engaged with one another for thousands of years already, and the Awakened are even <i>more </i>likely to have been so. Just a note about them.<br /> <br /> Also I have to offer some discomfort with the stated themes, or at least their phrasing. I wish I could articulate it succinctly, but I feel the &quot;denial of civilization&quot; is sorta weird. There was plenty of civilization there <i>before </i>the Leopold went looking for his slice of the African cake, even though violence in the area obviously doesn't begin with the arrival of Belgium. I'm just saying, refining those themes to sound less... Colonialist? Might be a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 02-12-2016, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T15:11:14-08:00","id":828973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/828221-gathering-ideas-for-a-dark-era-could-use-some-some-discussion?p=828958#post828958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think something worth keeping in mind about the Awakened is that Dave has implied the Awakened of Europe were well aware of their native counterparts in the Americas via the Astral Realm, so I really don't think it makes much sense for there to be African Mages entirely cut off from the Diamond.<br /> <br /> There might be those who refused involvement, or it might be that those members of the Diamond who were already present have to navigate the situation, but Africans and Europeans have been engaged with one another for thousands of years already, and the Awakened are even <i>more </i>likely to have been so. Just a note about them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was leaning towards a &quot;aware of the Diamond and sharing a history with them&quot; as well<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/828221-gathering-ideas-for-a-dark-era-could-use-some-some-discussion?p=828958#post828958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I have to offer some discomfort with the stated themes, or at least their phrasing. I wish I could articulate it succinctly, but I feel the &quot;denial of civilization&quot; is sorta weird. There was plenty of civilization there <i>before </i>the Leopold went looking for his slice of the African cake, even though violence in the area obviously doesn't begin with the arrival of Belgium. I'm just saying, refining those themes to sound less... Colonialist? Might be a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>That indeed was not the intended feeling nor an implication that the denial of civilization is something endemic to Congo. I fully intend to describe the native cultures and kingdoms (the books I use have bookmarks put there just for those chapters), with all their achievements. The idea was that in the specific window of time of Leopold's rule it was far too easy, for everyone, to distance themselves from civilization and forget what empathy means, because of the context created in the first place by the colonialists. But hey, a weird phrasing is a weird phrasing and if that's the message it conveys, I'll change it for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-12-2016, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T16:22:49-08:00","id":829012,"title":"","content":"Ok, I altered the Theme a bit. Changed the name, modified many sentences and added a few new ones. It should feel less, well, let's say problematic. If that's not the case, don't hesitate to tell me: the colonialist vibe is something I absolutely want to avoid, under all aspects.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I was thinking that, considering that the Congo Free State was one of the first places where the industrial machine was used as a justification and, at the same time, ispiration for the sort of cold-blooded atrocities that characterized the 20th century, it would be fertile ground for the God-Machine's methods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-12-2016, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T18:06:44-08:00","id":829052,"title":"","content":"A suggestion why not add unusual supernatural such as the strix or idigam as well some chronicles of darkness horrors you could aslo describe how the supernatural are affected by the atrocities of congo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T22:36:17-08:00","id":829133,"title":"","content":"Having theme of <i>&quot;Savagery Hidden Within&quot; </i>I would:<ul><li>Made for vampires some interesting Gangrel Bloodline, based on localized cultures. Returning &quot;colonists&quot; are taking this particular Curse with them to civilization.</li> <li>One werewolf front, I would think if we could not made some local Changing Breed - weregorillas? - that fight with Uratha settlers. Also, if wolves were population then - native Forsaken are very much degenerated, their Harmony is very low on the Spirits side. And I wanted to run <b>Wolf Man</b> scenario were white European goes to &quot;wild country&quot; and brought back shapeshifting curse with him.</li> </ul> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kQQfoIy7SNI\" data-code=\"kQQfoIy7SNI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/kQQfoIy7SNI/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><ul><li>For mages, local offshoots ( and fan 2ED write-ups ) for the <i>Devourers of the Flesh</i> and <i>Tamers of Blood</i> should nicely setup us within the theme. Add some Time Before ruin connected to &quot;barbarian practice&quot; and we are ready.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li>Prometheans could have some bestial Linage - or maybe some local variants, based on very much violent Generative Act - need to see 2ED on this matter before. Regional Aurum, under mimicking humans is <i>very</i> unsettling. More, Created learn here to steal Vitroil from one another, like Pandoran do this.</li> <li>Hunters, on both sides of conflict, are going more and more out of proportions. Slashers are created on massive scale, people are dead in thousands, monsters are praying on everything. Hunters should answer in their Vigil here &quot;What are you ready to do to other beings?&quot;</li> <li>Beasts just need to survive in this hell hole other game lines build for them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T08:34:43-08:00","id":829261,"title":"","content":"I've never read the Heart of Darkness and don't know much about the time, but color me interested- especially about Mokole mbembe and its place in the setting. Before starting to work on other supernaturals, I suggest first developing what is special about this place and this time for Beasts- my favorite Dark Eras or location settings present unique phenomena, beings or character options, some may be temporary and others may leave deep scars for all eternity. Any thoughts how to represent the way the Primordial Dream mix with the real world or how the local Beast society is structured?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T10:18:38-08:00","id":829299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/828221-gathering-ideas-for-a-dark-era-could-use-some-some-discussion?p=829133#post829133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having theme of <i>&quot;Savagery Hidden Within&quot; </i>I would:[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're aiming at but I'd rather keep the focus on how the events happened because of human actions and that supernaturals have no more influence over them than anybody else.<br /> <br /> Aside from the fact that this is a Beast's Era and that they should have a central place, I think that the supernaturals, both native and foreign, should have to face the same moral dilemma that everybody does and deal with its consequences, not to mention the effects the colonization has on the surroundings. Werewolves have to patch up the Shadow and not become mindless predators, Vampires can feed as much as they want if they abandon their moral qualms, the Mages typical hubris rears its ugly head if you consider the others inferior...you get the idea. If you're a native, you have to deal with fact that the westerners are destroying the status quo. If you're foreign, you have to decide whether you support the colonial methods or if it's up to you to do something.<br /> <br /> While there's plenty of room to feature some of the worst factions of the various gamelines, I think making all the monster unrepentant bastards responsible for the atrocities is a waste of potential and a disservice to the real events. The Congo Free State happened because of the evils of mankind and the supernaturals are no worse than many &quot;normal&quot; humans. The Era is going to be really dark and difficult to write properly (I'm talking about a <b>Wraith: </b><b>Charnel Houses of Europe </b>degree of difficulty), but I think that adapting the supernaturals to the setting and not the reverse is the right way to go.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/828221-gathering-ideas-for-a-dark-era-could-use-some-some-discussion?p=829261#post829261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never read the Heart of Darkness and don't know much about the time, but color me interested- especially about Mokole mbembe and its place in the setting. Before starting to work on other supernaturals, I suggest first developing what is special about this place and this time for Beasts- my favorite Dark Eras or location settings present unique phenomena, beings or character options, some may be temporary and others may leave deep scars for all eternity. Any thoughts how to represent the way the Primordial Dream mix with the real world or how the local Beast society is structured?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I completely agree. That's something I appreciated myself in the &quot;canon&quot; Dark Eras. I have many ideas but nothing too definite. Pathways to the Primordial Dream that open spontaneusly, normal people (and other supernaturals?) that become subject to Hungers and/or become their living embodiment, vivid nightmares, the risk to have your soul replaced with a Chamber when losing Integrity and release it in the material world upon death, there are tales of the Dark Mother roaming around... Many, little ideas that I'm thinking about.<br /> <br /> I do have a picture in mind of the local Beast society, but it's just a preliminar idea. Something along the lines of a &quot;feudal&quot; structure with each Beast associated to a given territory or tribe, with highly ritualized relationship between different Beasts. If there's a dispute they convoke a Beast of higher station as a judge and there are recurring Family meetings to discuss eventual problems. Mokole used to be quite elusive before the coming of the Belgians but now he's more willing to intervene. This solid structure has now to deal with foreign Beasts and how to make them fit to it. Foreign Beasts, on their hand, are not assured to care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-13-2016, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T11:48:06-08:00","id":829350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/828221-gathering-ideas-for-a-dark-era-could-use-some-some-discussion?p=829299#post829299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get what you're aiming at but I'd rather keep the focus on how the events happened because of human actions and that supernaturals have no more influence over them than anybody else.<br /> <br /> Aside from the fact that this is a Beast's Era and that they should have a central place, I think that the supernaturals, both native and foreign, should have to face the same moral dilemma that everybody does and deal with its consequences, not to mention the effects the colonization has on the surroundings. Werewolves have to patch up the Shadow and not become mindless predators, Vampires can feed as much as they want if they abandon their moral qualms, the Mages typical hubris rears its ugly head if you consider the others inferior...you get the idea. If you're a native, you have to deal with fact that the westerners are destroying the status quo. If you're foreign, you have to decide whether you support the colonial methods or if it's up to you to do something.<br /> <br /> While there's plenty of room to feature some of the worst factions of the various gamelines, I think making all the monster unrepentant bastards responsible for the atrocities is a waste of potential and a disservice to the real events. The Congo Free State happened because of the evils of mankind and the supernaturals are no worse than many &quot;normal&quot; humans. The Era is going to be really dark and difficult to write properly (I'm talking about a <b>Wraith: </b><b>Charnel Houses of Europe </b>degree of difficulty), but I think that adapting the supernaturals to the setting and not the reverse is the right way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I understand that, believe me. Only I point to you this - Kongo State is <i>living hell to humans</i>. Violance and tortures are on the rise, people do really nasty things to each other. And monsters <b>cannot stop them</b>. More - they entrenched in those astorcities. People die, they close one are suffering, supernaturals are on both side of conflicts. It's awakens demons in people. And living hell for humans, means <i>living hell for &quot;monsters&quot;</i>.<br /> <br /> In <b>Mage</b>, most of Left Handed are not &quot;evil for evil sake&quot; - they have they motives, they desires. Just Left Hand Path is immoral way to make them true. If you are in the constant war situation, you use extreme weapons. Okay, maybe not all do this. Maybe not even <i>most</i> do this. But war terrors stories are so often mentioned <i>because</i> they are true. People in times of war <i>makes</i> really horrible things to one another.<br /> <br /> And you <i>should</i> point out in your supernatural write-ups - in the end, &quot;monsters&quot; from <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> are only reflecting common humans fears, traumas and desires. It's double true in the game of <b>Beast</b> where you are Human Fear incarnated. <b>That's why you should point to the dark side of splats</b>. Maybe marking that not all of them do this. Maybe that even not <i>most</i> of them. But in the Hell that humans do, some &quot;monsters&quot; become <b><i>real</i> monsters</b>. They <b>must</b> do this, or they die.<br /> <br /> That's why I proposed Left Handed Legacies about human control and cannibalism - they are ways for mages to <i>survive hell and control war, all around them</i>. That's why I point that some Uratha should be thrown totally out of balance - they secretly despise humans and throw themselves on the Spirit side of their nature - that's, ironically, makes them even more monstrous. Supernaturals are <b><i>not</i> real source of problem</b> - they only <i>indicating </i>that this human war and situation only rising stakes out of proportion even in their kind. True monsters are humans - and it's <b><i>they</i></b> that changes splats in to extreme monsters.<br /> <br /> Unless you makes that humans hunt en mass on all supernaturals, I cannot see how to other way portray true savagery. Humans <b>push</b> splats to become monsters they told stories about. Supernatural do not have other way that embrace this. ( Even if some individuals in splats can try to fight this tendency )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-13-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T13:54:54-08:00","id":829398,"title":"","content":"If you put it this way, I'm quite more receptive to the idea. I still think it would be difficult to find a proper balance without going too far, but I'll keep this in mind for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T08:08:05-08:00","id":832527,"title":"","content":"More thoughts:<br /> <br /> - I'm not sure about the Family (Anakim or Makara, I guess) but I'm considering the idea of making Mokele-mbembe a Pigmy with Looking Presence. It might sound odd, but I think there's some coolness in making someone from an unusually short ethnic group a colossal dinosaur which gives vertigo even in human form. Makes for some nice descriptions and looks<br /> <br /> - There are many Bantu legends where people reach the heaven by climbing a tree and, sometimes, that tree is burned or cut down. I think I can work with that and the symbolism of the Exarch's Ladder.<br /> <br /> - Thinking about doing something with were-leopards and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leopard_Society\" target=\"_blank\">the Leopard Society</a>, not sure if the two should be connected though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T08:14:05-08:00","id":832531,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Mokele-mbembe possessing Looming Presence- makes perfect sense to me, especially since the first meeting with him (her?) would be exceedingly perplexing, and maybe almost nightmarish in its imagery, which is extremely appropriate.<br /> <br /> One thing to take into consideration is that at this point in time Mokele-mbembe would be <i>old</i>. The first legends about the creature are recorded around 1776","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T08:15:35-08:00","id":832532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/828221-gathering-ideas-for-a-dark-era-could-use-some-some-discussion?p=832531#post832531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Mokele-mbembe possessing Looming Presence- makes perfect sense to me, especially since the first meeting with him (her?) would be exceedingly perplexing, and maybe almost nightmarish in its imagery, which is extremely appropriate.<br /> <br /> One thing to take into consideration is that at this point in time Mokele-mbembe would be <i>old</i>. The first legends about the creature are recorded around 1776</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which would make the Beast powerful, as having a greater Lair means a longer life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T09:06:31-08:00","id":832549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/828221-gathering-ideas-for-a-dark-era-could-use-some-some-discussion?p=832532#post832532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Which would make the Beast powerful, as having a greater Lair means a longer life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really old and powerful, yes. I was aiming at Lair 9-10. <br /> <br /> He's (she?) a cumbersome presence. Native Beasts find him alien and terrifying, the king of the river that deserves respect but they can't really find a connection with (many of them are secretly glad he tends to mind his own business), while foreign ones have to be very careful when he's around.<br /> <br /> On his part, it means that most of his bonds with his mortal life are gone (that's why he was making all the arrangements to become Incarnate) but that the events of colonization who made him reconsider are putting him through an emotional turmoil. He thought he had left humanity behind long ago, but it seems he's not ready yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T19:33:59-08:00","id":832956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/828221-gathering-ideas-for-a-dark-era-could-use-some-some-discussion?p=832527#post832527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- There are many Bantu legends where people reach the heaven by climbing a tree and, sometimes, that tree is burned or cut down. I think I can work with that and the symbolism of the Exarch's Ladder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, but I would wait a few weeks for the <b>Dark Eras</b>. In <i>Neolithic Mage</i> we will have a much more clear image how mages worked before Great Cults and Orders coming from Hellenisation Era - ergo, how Nameless around world survive to Age of Exploration colonisation by Western World and European mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T01:08:47-08:00","id":833104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/828221-gathering-ideas-for-a-dark-era-could-use-some-some-discussion?p=832956#post832956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting, but I would wait a few weeks for the <b>Dark Eras</b>. In <i>Neolithic Mage</i> we will have a much more clear image how mages worked before Great Cults and Orders coming from Hellenisation Era - ergo, how Nameless around world survive to Age of Exploration colonisation by Western World and European mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, I won't start writing this until quite far in the future. I'm beginning to order the ideas and using this thread to help my brain work and solve many doubts and issues but:<br /> <br /> - I'll wait to see all the Dark Eras, with an eye for the Mutapa Empire for obvious reasons<br /> - It's a big project and I'm still somewhat burned out from my last one, so I'll need some time to find the force of will needed to start it.<br /> <br /> For now, I'm happy to discuss the various ideas and listen to your feedback so I can have a solid base to start from the day I start writing. It already proved to be quite useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}